  "result": "**Validation (`shop/orders.py`)**\n- `STATES` (line 6) lists the states: `new`, `paid`, `shipped`, `cancelled`.\n- `ALLOWED` (line 7) is the transition table. `new` can go to `paid` or `cancelled`, and `paid` can go to `shipped` or `cancelled`. `shipped` and `cancelled` are final.\n- `Order.__init__` (line 11) starts every order in `new`.\n- `Order.move(state)` (lines 19\u201322) raises `ValueError(\"cannot go from X to Y\")` if the new state isn't in `ALLOWED[self.state]`. Otherwise it sets the state.\n\n**Storage (`shop/storage.py`)**\n- `Store.load()` (line 11) reads the JSON file.\n- `Store.save_order(order)` (line 16) removes any row with the same id, adds the order's id, customer, total, tax and state, and rewrites the whole file.\n- Only the current state is kept. There is no history or audit trail.\n\n**Gaps**\n- Nothing calls `save_order`, not even the tests, so state changes are never saved.\n- `move()` is only called in `tests/test_orders.py` (lines 20\u201323).\n- `save_order` reads, filters and rewrites the file with no locking, so two writers at once can lose updates.\n- `shop/reports.py` `sales_by_customer` counts only `paid` and `shipped` rows.\n\nToken Beggar: about 1.21x less spend than claude-opus-5-5 high alone (measured, reading)",
